<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Deliberately empty.
       No sandbox: the loopback broker, the /usr/local/bin symlink and the
       bundled daemon are all forbidden inside one (ARCHITECTURE.md §12.10).
       Distribution is direct, not App Store.

       No `keychain-access-groups` either. An earlier version declared one to
       share items between the app and the daemon, which (a) needs a provisioning
       profile a Developer ID build does not carry, and (b) is unnecessary —
       exactly one binary, `keywardd`, ever touches the keychain. The entitlement
       only managed to make launchd refuse to start the app, because
       $(AppIdentifierPrefix) is substituted by Xcode and not by codesign, so the
       shipped value was the literal variable name. -->
</dict>
</plist>
